Subject: [PATCH 0/2] media: i2c: add Samsung S5K4H8 image sensor

Hi,

This series adds a DT binding and a V4L2 sub-device driver for the
Samsung S5K4H8 8 MP raw Bayer sensor (MIPI CSI-2, CCI/I2C).

Hardware:
 - Chip id 0x4088 at register 0x0000
 - 4-lane CSI-2 at 280 MHz (560 Mbps/lane), 24 MHz MCLK
 - Modes: 3264x2448 SGRBG10, and 1632x1224 2x2 binning
 - Stream on/off: 8-bit write to 0x0100 (0x01 / 0x00)

Implementation notes:
 - Register tables are adapted from the Rockchip vendor driver
   (GPL-2.0, Copyright (C) 2017 Fuzhou Rockchip Electronics Co., Ltd.).
   I/O goes through v4l2-cci.
 - Active-state subdev API (init_state, enable_streams). set_fmt and
   get_selection take struct v4l2_subdev_client_info, which this tree
   requires. In-kernel callers pass NULL.
 - Crop selection exposes the full pixel array. Binning is 2x2 of that
   array, not a windowed crop.
 - Power sequence: supplies, then MCLK, then XSHUTDOWN deassert and
   settle.

Base this series on https://git.linuxtv.org/media.git branch next at
aa0f4c41d487 ("media: ipu6: Enable snooping on ipu7 isys buffers").
That repository has no master branch. The old media_tree.git master
line in nearby MAINTAINERS entries is historical context only.

Non-goals: board DTS, OTP/AWB, H/V flip, test pattern.

Tested on Motorola Moto E4 (perry / MSM8917) with mainline-track CAMSS
and libcamera Simple pipeline:
 - rear sensor about 24 fps at 3264x2448 SGRBG10
 - v4l2-compliance on the sensor subdev: 46/46, 0 failures, 0 warnings

The phone capture predates the client-info callback argument. That
argument is unused; behavior is otherwise unchanged. The series was
compile-tested with W=1 on this base.

Board DTS is not included. It can follow once the binding is accepted.

Please review.

Thanks,
Aneesh

